From 8772b37fa15ce409fec6914ba887e7e2389e7c8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Trotter <33046718+sjtrotter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:49:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] RDP: preserve protected RDPW settings

Azure Virtual Desktop publishes protected connection files (.rdpw) whose
settings and signature the generic Remmina .rdp importer does not model.
Importing one produced a profile that could not reach the AVD gateway.

Read the protected file exactly once at import time through a descriptor
opened with O_NOFOLLOW, require a regular file of at most 1 MiB, and keep
the bytes (base64) in the profile as "rdpw_data". The generic fields are
imported from that same buffer, so the file is never re-read and a later
change to it cannot alter what was accepted. The importer also learns the
"redirectsmartcards" spelling used by AVD and maps "enablerdsaadauth:i:1"
to the "aad" security setting.

Before connecting, the buffer is filtered through an explicit allowlist of
AVD routing and authentication keys and only that filtered text is handed
to FreeRDP's native connection-file parser, which populates the live
rdpSettings. Lines starting with "/" are rejected because FreeRDP treats
them as embedded command-line arguments. The plugin-level parse happens
once, in remmina_rdp_main(), rather than for every queued input event.

Tested with FreeRDP 3.31.0. The APIs used are present in FreeRDP
3.30.0; FreeRDP 3.31.0 or newer is only required for complete
sovereign-cloud support when SSO-MIB is enabled.

This change was prepared with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic) and was
reviewed and tested by the author.
